1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:04,480
On October 15, 2026, Tesla demonstrated something that

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,820
appeared to defy the laws of physics. A

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:10,240
roadster accelerated toward a massive curved ramp, climbed

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,880
almost vertically, continued driving while completely upside down,

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:16,340
and then launched into the air. But instead

6
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:20,000
of falling uncontrollably, it rotated through 180 degrees,

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,560
corrected its orientation, and landed on its wheels.

8
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,800
Think about what this requires. How can a

9
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,310
car remain attached to a surface when gravity

10
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:30,300
is pulling it away? How can it rotate

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,740
its entire body while airborne? And how can

12
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:35,190
a vehicle weighing nearly two tons survive such

13
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:37,620
a landing? To answer these questions, we're going

14
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:41,670
to reconstruct the manoeuvre using mathematical equations, three-dimensional

15
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:45,440
engineering models, and physics simulations, and we'll discover

16
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,880
that this apparently impossible stunt is actually a

17
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:52,260
combination of several well-understood physical principles. Let's begin

18
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:55,590
with the vehicle itself. Tesla's system combines electric

19
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:59,580
motors, four powerful suction fans, deployable aerodynamic skirts,

20
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:02,570
and a collection of compressed gas thrusters. The

21
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:04,920
fans control how strongly the car presses against

22
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,460
a surface, the thrusters control its motion when

23
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,960
the wheels can no longer provide support. For

24
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,760
our calculations, let's assume a vehicle mass of

25
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:16,310
1700 kg, approximately the reported target mass of

26
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:18,830
the roadster. The force of gravity acting on

27
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:20,700
this mass is given by mass multiplied by

28
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:26,440
gravitational acceleration, that gives us approximately 16,700 newtons.

29
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,430
In ordinary driving, the road balances this downward

30
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:31,980
force through its normal reaction, but during Tesla's

31
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:34,350
manoeuvre, both the direction and magnitude of the

32
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:38,370
contact forces change dramatically, and understanding that change

33
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:41,450
is the key to the entire demonstration. Consider

34
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:44,280
an ordinary car travelling up an inclined road.

35
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,000
Gravity acts vertically downward, but we can divide

36
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,020
it into two components. The perpendicular component is

37
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,250
mass times gravity times the cosine of the

38
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:55,620
incline angle. The parallel component is mass times

39
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:58,140
gravity times the sine of that angle. The

40
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,930
parallel component is what pulls the car backward

41
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:03,110
down the slope. To overcome this force, the

42
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:05,920
tyres must generate sufficient traction, but traction is

43
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,910
limited by friction. A maximum friction force equals

44
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:11,610
the coefficient of friction multiplied by the normal

45
00:02:11,610 --> 00:02:14,870
force. Combining these equations gives us a simple

46
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:17,470
condition. The tangent of the incline angle must

47
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:20,420
not exceed the friction coefficient. If the friction

48
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:23,050
coefficient is 1, the car can theoretically resist

49
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:25,630
sliding on an incline of up to 45

50
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:28,170
degrees. As the angle increases, gravity pulls more

51
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:30,560
strongly down the slope, while the normal force

52
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:34,630
decreases. At 90 degrees, the gravitational contribution to

53
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:37,140
the normal force becomes 0. And without some

54
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,840
additional mechanism, the tyres cannot generate the traction

55
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,760
required to climb a vertical wall. Making the

56
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:45,230
motors more powerful cannot solve this problem by

57
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:47,830
itself. The car needs another source of normal

58
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:51,190
force, and that's exactly what Tesla engineered. Beneath

59
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:54,400
the roadster are four electrically powered suction fans.

60
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,710
Tesla's engineers reported that these fans are rated

61
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:59,900
at approximately 20 kilowatts each. The fans remove

62
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,510
air from beneath the vehicle, while deployable skirts

63
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:04,970
help restrict the flow of surrounding air into

64
00:03:04,970 --> 00:03:08,030
the low pressure region. This creates a pressure

65
00:03:08,030 --> 00:03:09,840
difference between the two sides of the car.

66
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,830
Higher atmospheric pressure pushes the vehicle toward the

67
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:16,070
road. The resulting force equals the pressure difference

68
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:18,380
multiplied by the effective area. Tesla claims its

69
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:20,680
system can generate a suction force, equivalent to

70
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:24,620
approximately twice the vehicle's weight. For our 1700

71
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:28,900
kilogram model, that's around 33,400 newtons. Now suppose

72
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:31,920
the effective suction area is two square meters.

73
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,390
Dividing the force by the area gives a

74
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:38,330
required pressure difference of approximately 16.7 kilopascals. That's

75
00:03:38,330 --> 00:03:41,470
only about 16% of standard atmospheric pressure. So

76
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:43,480
the system doesn't need to create a perfect

77
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:45,790
vacuum. It simply needs to maintain a substantial

78
00:03:45,790 --> 00:03:48,900
pressure difference across a large enough surface. Now

79
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,870
look at how this changes tyre grip. On

80
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:53,250
a straight incline, the normal force becomes the

81
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:56,720
gravitational normal component, plus the suction force. At

82
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:00,030
90 degrees, gravity contributes nothing to this normal

83
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:02,210
load, but the fans can still press the

84
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:05,290
tyres against the wall. With a friction coefficient

85
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:08,050
of one, our simulated car would have approximately

86
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:12,330
33,400 newtons of available traction. Gravity pulls it

87
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:16,080
downward, with only 16,700 newtons. So in this

88
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,630
idealised case, the available traction is twice the

89
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:21,530
force needed to hold the car stationary. That's

90
00:04:21,530 --> 00:04:23,600
how the roadster can climb a nearly vertical

91
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:26,230
surface. But what happens when the road curves

92
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:28,990
beyond vertical and the car becomes inverted? At

93
00:04:28,990 --> 00:04:30,880
the top of an inverted road, gravity is

94
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,560
no longer pressing the car against the surface.

95
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:35,820
It's pulling the car away. If the car

96
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:38,440
is stationary, suction must exceed its weight to

97
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:41,110
maintain contact. With a suction force equal to

98
00:04:41,110 --> 00:04:43,090
twice the weight, the remaining contact force is

99
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:46,990
approximately one vehicle weight. But the demonstration also

100
00:04:46,990 --> 00:04:49,920
involves a curved trajectory and curved motion introduces

101
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:54,830
centripetal acceleration. Its magnitude equals velocity squared, divided

102
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:57,900
by the local radius of curvature. Multiplying by

103
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,031
mass gives the net inward force required to

104
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:03,010
follow the curve. Consider a simplified circular loop,

105
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:05,280
with the car moving along its inside surface,

106
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,650
at the very top, the inward direction points

107
00:05:07,650 --> 00:05:10,990
downward. The radial force equation combines the road's

108
00:05:10,990 --> 00:05:14,660
normal reaction, gravity, and suction. Rearranging it gives

109
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:17,110
the normal force as suction plus mass times

110
00:05:17,110 --> 00:05:20,830
velocity squared divided by radius. Minus the vehicle's

111
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:23,520
weight. Let's assume a curved radius of 12

112
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,650
meters and a speed of 12 meters per

113
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:30,590
second. The required centripetal force is approximately 20,400

114
00:05:30,590 --> 00:05:33,370
newtons. Combining this with our assumed suction and

115
00:05:33,370 --> 00:05:36,110
gravitational forces gives a road contact reaction of

116
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:40,060
about 37,000 newtons. This shows why the geometry

117
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:43,850
matters. Contact force depends on suction, gravity, speed,

118
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:46,170
and the local curvature of the road. And

119
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:49,810
because centripetal acceleration scales with velocity squared, changing

120
00:05:49,810 --> 00:05:52,520
speed can dramatically alter the forces acting on

121
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,870
the vehicle. Now the roadster reaches the end

122
00:05:54,870 --> 00:05:56,700
of the ramp as the vehicle separates from

123
00:05:56,700 --> 00:06:00,270
the surface. The road's contact force disappears. The

124
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:02,990
car becomes a freely moving rigid body. Tesla

125
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:05,670
solves the next problem using compressed gas thrusters

126
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:09,510
developed with technology from SpaceX. The reported flight

127
00:06:09,510 --> 00:06:12,980
configuration contains 10 nozzles and approximately 250 kg

128
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:16,900
of compressed gas. When pressurized gas escapes through

129
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:19,800
a nozzle, it carries momentum in one direction.

130
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,980
Conservation of momentum produces a reaction force in

131
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:25,110
the opposite direction. The rocket thrust equation relates

132
00:06:25,110 --> 00:06:27,840
this force to gas mass flow, exhaust velocity,

133
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:30,910
and nozzle exit pressure. For a simplified model,

134
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:32,810
thrust equals mass flow rate multiplied by an

135
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:36,720
effective exhaust velocity. Suppose we want 20,000 newtons

136
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,850
of force, with an effective exhaust velocity of

137
00:06:38,850 --> 00:06:43,270
600 m/s. That requires approximately 33 kg of

138
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:46,190
gas every second. This explains why the thrusters

139
00:06:46,190 --> 00:06:48,670
can produce enormous forces, but only for short

140
00:06:48,670 --> 00:06:51,800
periods. The stored gas is finite, and pressure

141
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:54,580
decreases as it is released. These systems are

142
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:58,480
therefore particularly useful for rapid acceleration, trajectory corrections,

143
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:01,380
and short bursts of rotational control. Now consider

144
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:03,640
the car while it's upside down in mid-air.

145
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:07,040
To land correctly, it must rotate approximately 180

146
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,620
degrees, but applying a force through the center

147
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:12,560
of mass only accelerates the vehicle. To rotate

148
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:15,110
it, we need torque. Torque is the cross

149
00:07:15,110 --> 00:07:17,340
product of the position vector and the applied

150
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:20,400
force. For rotation around a principal axis, torque

151
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:24,160
equals moment of inertia multiplied by angular acceleration.

152
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:27,060
Let's model a role around the car's longitudinal

153
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:29,870
axis. Assume its moment of inertia is 800

154
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:32,420
kg m2, and suppose we want to complete

155
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:35,751
a half revolution in 1.6 seconds, beginning and

156
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:38,780
ending with zero role velocity. We can divide

157
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:41,410
the motion into two equal phases. During the

158
00:07:41,410 --> 00:07:44,770
first half, the thrusters accelerate the rotation. During

159
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:46,880
the second half, they reverse the torque and

160
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:49,900
reduce the angular velocity to zero. For constant

161
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:53,960
acceleration and deceleration, the required angular acceleration magnitude

162
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:56,950
is four times the rotation angle, divided by

163
00:07:56,950 --> 00:07:59,990
the total time squared. Substituting pi radians and

164
00:07:59,990 --> 00:08:03,920
1.6 seconds gives approximately 4.9 radians per second

165
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:07,200
squared. Multiplying by the moment of inertia gives

166
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:11,440
a torque requirement of roughly 3,900 Newton meters.

167
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,430
Now imagine two thrusters producing equal and opposite

168
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:17,160
vertical forces on opposite sides of the chassis,

169
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:20,290
with an effective separation of 1.5 meters, each

170
00:08:20,290 --> 00:08:24,290
thruster needs approximately 2,600 newtons to create the

171
00:08:24,290 --> 00:08:27,240
required couple. Their forces nearly cancel as a

172
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:30,080
net vertical force, while their torques add. And

173
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,800
by reversing that torque halfway through the manoeuvre,

174
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:35,390
the car can reach an upright orientation with

175
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:38,790
approximately zero angular velocity. The real manoeuvre is

176
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:41,550
more complex, because pitch, roll and york can

177
00:08:41,550 --> 00:08:44,200
interact. In a complete simulation, we must use

178
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:47,980
the vehicle's three-dimensional inertia tensor and calculate angular

179
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:50,530
motion along all three axes, but rotating the

180
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:52,750
car is only part of the challenge. The

181
00:08:52,750 --> 00:08:55,550
system must also control the position and velocity

182
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:58,310
of its centre of mass. Every thruster contributes

183
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:00,550
a force, and depending on its location, a

184
00:09:00,550 --> 00:09:03,420
torque. The total force determines the car's linear

185
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:06,720
acceleration. The total torque determines how its angular

186
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:09,860
momentum changes. A flight controller must estimate the

187
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:14,440
vehicle's current position, velocity, orientation, and angular velocity.

188
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:16,690
It then calculates the force and torque needed

189
00:09:16,690 --> 00:09:19,910
to follow a desired trajectory. Finally, it determines

190
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:22,400
which nozzles should fire, and for how long.

191
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:25,550
This process is called control allocation. Tesla has

192
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:28,110
not published its exact control algorithms, but the

193
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:30,670
underlying mathematics is similar to that used in

194
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:34,370
spacecraft attitude control and robotic flight systems. The

195
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:35,990
goal is to reach the ground with the

196
00:09:35,990 --> 00:09:39,880
correct orientation, a manageable descent velocity, and minimal

197
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:43,360
unwanted rotation. Now imagine the roadster descending toward

198
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,480
the ground, suppose it falls from rest through

199
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:49,980
20 metres, without any thruster assistance. Conservation of

200
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:53,090
energy tells us that gravitational potential energy becomes

201
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:55,600
kinetic energy, and resulting impact speed is the

202
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,950
square root of twice gravitational acceleration multiplied by

203
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:02,910
height. That gives approximately 19.8 metres per second,

204
00:10:02,910 --> 00:10:05,840
or more than 70 kilometres per hour downward.

205
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:08,280
To avoid a destructive landing, the car must

206
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:11,120
reduce that velocity. The vertical equation of motion

207
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:14,750
is simple. Mass times vertical acceleration equals upward

208
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:18,360
directed thrust minus gravitational weight. For our simulated

209
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:21,610
vehicle, a thrust of 16.7 kN would balance

210
00:10:21,610 --> 00:10:25,280
gravity, but balancing gravity does not automatically stop

211
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:28,140
a falling object. To actually slow its descent,

212
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:31,350
thrust must exceed weight. Now consider a simplified

213
00:10:31,350 --> 00:10:34,630
landing simulation. The vehicle begins falling from rest

214
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:36,620
at 20 metres. We allow it to fall

215
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:39,190
freely through the first 10 metres. This downward

216
00:10:39,190 --> 00:10:42,290
velocity reaches approximately 14 metres per second, then

217
00:10:42,290 --> 00:10:45,170
we activate the braking thrusters. To reduce that

218
00:10:45,170 --> 00:10:47,850
velocity to zero over the remaining 10 metres,

219
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:50,220
the car needs a net upward acceleration of

220
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:53,980
approximately 1g. The thrusters must therefore generate approximately

221
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:57,690
twice the vehicle's weight, that's 33.4 kilonewtons of

222
00:10:57,690 --> 00:11:00,470
upward thrust. In this idealised scenario, the car

223
00:11:00,470 --> 00:11:03,520
could theoretically reduce its vertical speed to zero

224
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:06,930
before touching the ground. The actual demonstration involved

225
00:11:06,930 --> 00:11:10,180
a different initial velocity, changing thrust directions, and

226
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,990
a more complicated trajectory, but the principle is

227
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:15,350
the same. The landing system must remove enough

228
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:18,040
downward momentum before the wheels make contact. So

229
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,990
did Tesla create a car that breaks the

230
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:23,590
laws of physics? No. The demonstration combines several

231
00:11:23,590 --> 00:11:27,480
established physical principles in an extraordinary way. Pressure

232
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:31,620
differences create artificial grip. Friction transfers propulsion forces

233
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:34,420
to the road. The triple acceleration governs the

234
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:38,210
curved inverted trajectory. Compressed gas thrusters generate impulse

235
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:41,380
and rotational torque, and carefully directed thrust reduces

236
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:44,710
the car's landing velocity. But performing this manoeuvre

237
00:11:44,710 --> 00:11:46,180
once is not the same as making it

238
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:49,840
safe, efficient, or practical for everyday transportation. The

239
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:53,010
system still faces limitations in stored gas, pressure

240
00:11:53,010 --> 00:11:56,470
loss, fan ceiling, energy consumption, and flight control

241
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:58,890
precision. We also don't yet have the complete

242
00:11:58,890 --> 00:12:03,230
engineering data required to independently reconstruct Tesla's exact

243
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:06,550
trajectory, but the underlying physics is clear. Tesla

244
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:09,460
didn't escape gravity. It used pressure, momentum, and

245
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:12,000
controlled forces to overcome the limitations of an

246
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,740
ordinary car. And sometimes, what looks like impossible

247
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:18,120
physics is simply mathematics brought to life.

